        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "69e3899f-c1a0-57dd-9eec-176a2917b261",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Matthieu Vaxivière, Marlon Stöckinger\n- Organizations: Tech 1 Racing, Lotus F1 Junior Team, Status Grand Prix\n- Competitions: French F4, V de V Endurance Cup, French GT, 2e Grand Prix Électrique, Formula Renault 2.0 Alps, Formula Renault 2.0 Eurocup, Formula Renault 3.5 Series, GP3 Series, World Series by Renault\n- Places: Manila\n- Roles: Racing drivers\n\nFacts:\n- Matthieu Vaxivière was the 2011 French F4 champion.\n- In 2012, Matthieu Vaxivière raced in the V de V Endurance Cup, French GT, and 2e Grand Prix Électrique.\n- In 2012, Matthieu Vaxivière finished 14th in the Formula Renault 2.0 Alps season and 29th in the Formula Renault 2.0 Eurocup while driving for Tech 1 Racing.\n- In 2012, Marlon Stöckinger raced for Status Grand Prix in the GP3 Series.\n- In 2013, Matthieu Vaxivière finished 10th in the Formula Renault 2.0 Eurocup and 18th in Formula Renault 2.0 Alps.\n- In 2013, Marlon Stöckinger drove for Lotus F1 Team Juniors in the World Series by Renault.\n- In 2014, Matthieu Vaxivière was assigned as a driver for the Lotus F1 Junior Team and competed in the Formula Renault 3.5 Series alongside Marlon Stöckinger.\n- Marlon Alexander Stöckinger was born on 4 April 1991 in Manila and is a Filipino racing driver.",
